loss_keeper: image built (19 expected lines)
=== round 1: running -- the source holds a ledger, the keeper takes a copy ===
disk: round 1 -- the source's /data/ledger holds 3 files besides the note, 1 directory, 300060 bytes
disk: round 1 -- the keeper's /data/copy is, file for file, that directory: yes
disk: round 1 -- the source's record holds 2 entries, the keeper's 1
=== the first roll: both records, collected from their disks ===
first: roll: fleet boutique -- 2 members, 2 keep a record; as of 2026-11-08 09:00 UTC, by the caller's clock
first: roll: this fleet takes its time from nobody, so no entry is dated: every record below is ORDERED and UNDATED
first: roll: this is the first roll: there is nothing to compare it with
first: roll: depot -- 2 entries, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP1); head H1, and no secret took part
first: roll: depot -- every entry is ORDERED and UNDATED: the fleet takes its time from nobody
first: roll: annex -- 1 entry, from its first, in order, each signed by the key enrolled for it (fingerprint FP2); head H2, and no secret took part
first: roll: annex -- every entry is ORDERED and UNDATED: the fleet takes its time from nobody
first: roll: 2 of 2 records held
first: roll: clean: every record that should be there is, and is its member's, in order from its first entry
first: roll: written to zig-out/loss/first.roll: the next roll is compared with it (--since)
first: exit 0
=== round 2: the loss -- both machines run, and the source is destroyed while they do ===
drill: both machines are running and each has written this boot in its record: source yes, keeper yes
drill: the source is destroyed -- its emulator killed outright: no running; disk images of it left: 0
drill: what the scene keeps of it, read before the loss and held by no member: its directory as round 1's disk held it, and its record as the first roll was brought it
drill: after the loss the keeper went on asking, and its disk came to say its last attempt was silent: yes
drill: the keeper's emulator is still running: yes (a running emulator is not a working machine: the line above is the keeper's own word)
=== the rest: what the keeper's disk holds after the loss ===
disk: the keeper's /data/copy holds 3 files besides the note, 1 directory, 300060 bytes
disk: it is, file for file, the ledger the source's disk held at round 1: yes
disk: /data/copy.last says: silent nobody answered at 10.30.0.1:7400
=== the host: the copy, checked by somebody who holds only the fleet file ===
kept: mirror: fleet boutique, MIRROR ledger_copy -- depot (enrolled as FP1) gives /data/ledger to annex (enrolled as FP2)
kept: mirror: zig-out/loss/k_r2/copy -- 4 files, 1 directory, 300066 bytes: every file matches the digest the source signed, and nothing else is there
kept: mirror: the listing was signed by FP1 for FP2, the two keys this fleet holds, and no secret took part
kept: exit 0
=== round 3: re-judged -- the keeper boots alone, with the source gone for good ===
disk: round 3 -- the keeper's /data/copy is the copy it held at the loss: yes
