=== what each machine said ===
running source: the source with the ledger, round 1:
source1: boot: harb init -- machine mirror_source (hosted / x86_64 / qemu_pc) -- pid 1
source1: boot: console /dev/ttyS0
source1: boot: mount proc at /proc -- done
source1: boot: mount sysfs at /sys -- done
source1: boot: mount devtmpfs at /dev -- done
source1: boot: mount ext4 at /data -- done
source1: boot: grant process (effectful)
source1: boot: grant filesystem (effectful)
source1: boot: grant network (effectful)
source1: boot: network lan -- eth0 up 10.30.0.1/24
source1: boot: identity -- ed25519, custody a file at /data/device.key -- already on this device, fingerprint FP1
source1: boot: mirror -- lan gives the files of /data/ledger on 10.30.0.1:7400, only to a request signed by the one device whose key it was told; the listing is signed with this device's key and cut for that device alone, and only the files ledger owns are given
source1: boot: confine -- enrol has no network of its own, ledger has no network of its own and no sight of the other worlds and no way to start one; what a world did not declare, the kernel does not give it
source1: boot: floor -- the machine is not a world's to change: none may mount or unmount, set the clock, load a module, rename the host, make or enter a namespace, trace another process, take a priority over the other worlds, or reboot the box
source1: boot: crypto -- the kernel answers a request for its crypto socket (AF_ALG) with EAFNOSUPPORT: it has none for a world to open, and the floor refuses one to every world besides
source1: boot: state -- ledger owns /data/ledger as clerk (2000:2000); each made, then read back as that identity's, mode 0700
source1: boot: start enrol -- pid N -- /harb attest --export
source1: attest mirror_source -- ed25519, fingerprint FP1
source1: enrol mirror_source ed25519 KEY1 -- KEY for this machine's MEMBER in a fleet
source1: attest: signed 21 bytes with this device's key and verified them against its public half
source1: attest: one bit flipped in the message, and the same signature is refused
source1: boot: enrol (pid N) exited 0
source1: boot: start ledger -- pid N -- /harb own /data/ledger -- as clerk (2000:2000)
source1: own: uid=2000 gid=2000
source1: own: /data/ledger -- wrote note and read it back (6 bytes)
source1: own: /data -- refused: AccessDenied
source1: own: / -- refused: AccessDenied
source1: own: this world wrote in its own directory and nowhere else
source1: boot: ledger (pid N) exited 0
source1: boot: judge -- the boot matches its expectation (/etc/expected, 20 lines)
source1: boot: journal -- /data/journal: 1 entry verified, entry 2 appended and signed (verdict matched)
source1: boot: every service has ended -- and this machine is still the mirror source of lan: a server stops when the machine stops, not when the asking does
